IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `itaa36-tfn`

-- Income Tax Assessment Act 1936 Part VA (tax file numbers) -- worked cases, from the seat of the person starting a job.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the deposited text (C2026C00333), never copied from the encoding's output.
--
-- Facts from the WA lives (workbench scenarios au/wa/cradle-to-grave-*):
--   chloe c020 (2018-03-14): turns 15; a tax file number and a casual job at a supermarket.
--   jake  k020 (2021-08-30): turns 15; a tax file number and no job yet.
--   daniel d012 (2012-10-15): turns 16; a tax file number; a casual job.
-- The lives give no more than that. The day each job begins, what each declaration says and when a number is passed on are
-- the encoder's, HYPOTHETICAL, and labelled where used. The lives are replayed on the 2026 compilation, not on Part VA as it
-- stood in 2012 or 2018.

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- chloe c020: applies for a TFN on 14 March 2018, the day she turns 15. HYPOTHETICAL: her casual job at the supermarket
-- begins on Monday 19 March 2018, and that day she gives the supermarket a TFN declaration saying her application is
-- pending. Her number arrives and she tells the supermarket on 2 April 2018.

-- Wages from the supermarket: she is a recipient (s 202A), whatever her age and even if nothing is withheld (s 202AA(a)).
#ASSERT `Am I a recipient of this payer` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I have to give this payer my TFN` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: I may make a TFN declaration to this payer, stating my TFN or that my application for one is pending, but Part VA does not require me to (s 202C(1))`

-- Her application: identity established, no earlier TFN, no interim notice in force: the Commissioner must issue one.
#ASSERT `What must the Commissioner do with my TFN application` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Commissioner must issue me a tax file number, by written notice of the number (s 202BA(1), (5))`

-- The 28 days after the pending statement of 19 March 2018 end on 16 April 2018 (s 202CB(3)).
#ASSERT `the last day to tell my payer my TFN` (Date 19 3 2018) EQUALS Date 16 4 2018

-- Effective on the approved form with the pending statement, and told on 2 April, within the 28 days: still effective on
-- 1 May 2018, after the 28 days, because s 202CB(3) never applied.
GIVEN `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `told` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day told` IS A DATE
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
`c020 pending declaration effective on` MEANS
    `Is my TFN declaration effective on a day` (Date 19 3 2018) `the day asked about` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `told` `the day told` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE

#ASSERT `c020 pending declaration effective on` (Date 19 3 2018) TRUE (Date 2 4 2018) EQUALS `answered` TRUE
#ASSERT `c020 pending declaration effective on` (Date 1 5 2018) TRUE (Date 2 4 2018) EQUALS `answered` TRUE
-- Counterfactual: she never tells the supermarket. Effective on the 28th day, not on the 29th.
#ASSERT `c020 pending declaration effective on` (Date 16 4 2018) FALSE (Date 1 1 2018) EQUALS `answered` TRUE
#ASSERT `c020 pending declaration effective on` (Date 17 4 2018) FALSE (Date 1 1 2018) EQUALS `answered` FALSE
-- Counterfactual: she tells them on 20 April 2018, after the 28 days: the statement has lapsed and the late number does not
-- revive it (she may make a new declaration, s 202CC).
#ASSERT `c020 pending declaration effective on` (Date 1 5 2018) TRUE (Date 20 4 2018) EQUALS `answered` FALSE

-- The supermarket must send her declaration on within 14 days: by 2 April 2018 (s 202CD(1)(b)).
#ASSERT `the last day for my payer to send on my TFN declaration` (Date 19 3 2018) EQUALS Date 2 4 2018

-- s 202CF: her pending declaration is effective at the end of the 14 days (2 April 2018), so no notice is due.
#ASSERT `By when must my employer notify the Commissioner that I made no TFN declaration` (Date 19 3 2018) TRUE (Date 19 3 2018) FALSE TRUE TRUE (Date 2 4 2018) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- Counterfactual: she makes no declaration: the supermarket must notify the Commissioner by 2 April 2018.
#ASSERT `By when must my employer notify the Commissioner that I made no TFN declaration` (Date 19 3 2018) FALSE (Date 1 1 2018) FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2018) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 2 4 2018)
-- Counterfactual: she makes it on 5 April 2018, after the 14 days: the notice was still due by 2 April 2018.
#ASSERT `By when must my employer notify the Commissioner that I made no TFN declaration` (Date 19 3 2018) TRUE (Date 5 4 2018) TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2018) FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 2 4 2018)
-- Counterfactual: no declaration, but an interim notice to the supermarket is in force on 2 April 2018 -- that alone is not a
-- declaration "in effect", so the notice is still due.
#ASSERT `By when must my employer notify the Commissioner that I made no TFN declaration` (Date 19 3 2018) FALSE (Date 1 1 2018) FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2018) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST (Date 2 4 2018)
-- Counterfactual: she gave the declaration to the Commissioner and the Tax Office passed her number on in the 14 days.
#ASSERT `By when must my employer notify the Commissioner that I made no TFN declaration` (Date 19 3 2018) FALSE (Date 1 1 2018) FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2018) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING

-- Counterfactual: she named the supermarket in her application and the Commissioner gave it an interim notice starting
-- 20 March 2018: in force for 28 days counting that day, to 16 April 2018 (s 202BD(2)).
#ASSERT `the last day the interim notice is in force` (Date 20 3 2018) EQUALS Date 16 4 2018
-- While it is in force, a declaration that states nothing is taken to state her TFN (s 202CB(4)).
#ASSERT `Is my TFN declaration effective on a day` (Date 19 3 2018) (Date 10 4 2018) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2018) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my TFN declaration effective on a day` (Date 19 3 2018) (Date 10 4 2018) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2018) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` FALSE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- jake k020: applies for a TFN on 30 August 2021, the day he turns 15, with no job.

-- No payer: not a recipient, and no declaration to make.
#ASSERT NOT `Am I a recipient of this payer` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Do I have to give this payer my TFN` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: I am not, and do not expect to be, a recipient of this payer, so Part VA gives me no TFN declaration to make to them`

-- Applying needs no job: the Commissioner must issue a number once satisfied of his identity.
#ASSERT `What must the Commissioner do with my TFN application` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Commissioner must issue me a tax file number, by written notice of the number (s 202BA(1), (5))`
-- Counterfactuals: identity not established; a number already issued.
#ASSERT `What must the Commissioner do with my TFN application` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the Commissioner may refuse it, because the Commissioner is not satisfied as to my true identity (s 202BA(2))`
#ASSERT `What must the Commissioner do with my TFN application` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse it, because I already have a tax file number or an interim notice about me is in force (s 202BA(3))`
-- Counterfactual: a second application while an interim notice about him is in force must be refused (s 202BA(3)(b)).
#ASSERT `What must the Commissioner do with my TFN application` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `the Commissioner must refuse it, because I already have a tax file number or an interim notice about me is in force (s 202BA(3))`

-- HYPOTHETICAL: no decision has come. The 28 days after 30 August 2021 end on 27 September 2021; he may give notice treating
-- the application as refused from 28 September 2021 (s 202BC(1)).
#ASSERT NOT `May I treat my TFN application as refused` (Date 30 8 2021) (Date 27 9 2021) FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `May I treat my TFN application as refused` (Date 30 8 2021) (Date 28 9 2021) FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `May I treat my TFN application as refused` (Date 30 8 2021) (Date 28 9 2021) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `May I treat my TFN application as refused` (Date 30 8 2021) (Date 28 9 2021) FALSE TRUE

-- HYPOTHETICAL: on 1 September 2021 he tells the Commissioner of a payer he did not name; at the end of 8 September 2021 the
-- payer is taken to be named in the application (s 202BD(6)).
#ASSERT `the day at whose end the payer is taken to be named` (Date 1 9 2021) EQUALS Date 8 9 2021

-- Review in the Tribunal (s 202F(1)): a refusal (actual or deemed), a cancellation, a s 202CE(3) notice; not a withdrawal.
#ASSERT `May I seek review of the decision about my TFN` `the Commissioner refused my application for a tax file number, or I treated it as refused under s 202BC`
#ASSERT `May I seek review of the decision about my TFN` `the Commissioner cancelled my tax file number as issued under an identity not my true identity`
#ASSERT `May I seek review of the decision about my TFN` `the Commissioner told my employer that the number in my TFN declaration is not my tax file number`
#ASSERT NOT `May I seek review of the decision about my TFN` `the Commissioner withdrew my tax file number and issued me a new one`

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- daniel d012: turns 16 on 15 October 2012 with a TFN. HYPOTHETICAL: his casual job begins that day and he gives his
-- employer a TFN declaration stating his number that day; his last pay is on 28 February 2013.

#ASSERT `Am I a recipient of this payer` TRUE FALSE

GIVEN `the day asked about` IS A DATE
      `approved form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `CE1 notice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `CE3 notice` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Answer` BOOLEAN
`d012 declaration effective on` MEANS
    `Is my TFN declaration effective on a day` (Date 15 10 2012) `the day asked about` `approved form` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2012) FALSE FALSE `CE1 notice` `CE3 notice`

#ASSERT `d012 declaration effective on` (Date 15 10 2012) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` TRUE
-- Not yet made the day before; not on the approved form; a s 202CE(3) notice has taken effect (s 202CE(6)).
#ASSERT `d012 declaration effective on` (Date 14 10 2012) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` FALSE
#ASSERT `d012 declaration effective on` (Date 15 10 2012) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` FALSE
#ASSERT `d012 declaration effective on` (Date 1 12 2012) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `answered` FALSE
-- The Commissioner gave his employer his correct number instead: regarded as always stating it (s 202CE(2)).
#ASSERT `d012 declaration effective on` (Date 1 12 2012) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `answered` TRUE

-- His employer must send the declaration on by 29 October 2012, and owes no s 202CF notice.
#ASSERT `the last day for my payer to send on my TFN declaration` (Date 15 10 2012) EQUALS Date 29 10 2012
#ASSERT `By when must my employer notify the Commissioner that I made no TFN declaration` (Date 15 10 2012) TRUE (Date 15 10 2012) TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2012) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

-- s 202CA: last paid 28 February 2013, so the declaration lasts to 28 February 2014 and not a day longer (s 202CA(1C)).
#ASSERT `Is my TFN declaration in effect on a day` (Date 15 10 2012) (Date 28 2 2014) FALSE TRUE (Date 28 2 2013) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Is my TFN declaration in effect on a day` (Date 15 10 2012) (Date 1 3 2014) FALSE TRUE (Date 28 2 2013) FALSE
-- Counterfactual: never paid: it lasts to 15 October 2013 (s 202CA(1B)).
#ASSERT `Is my TFN declaration in effect on a day` (Date 15 10 2012) (Date 15 10 2013) FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2012) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Is my TFN declaration in effect on a day` (Date 15 10 2012) (Date 16 10 2013) FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2012) FALSE
-- Counterfactual: replaced by a new declaration (s 202CA(1A)), or ended by a Commissioner's determination (s 202CA(2)).
#ASSERT NOT `Is my TFN declaration in effect on a day` (Date 15 10 2012) (Date 1 12 2012) TRUE TRUE (Date 28 11 2012) FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Is my TFN declaration in effect on a day` (Date 15 10 2012) (Date 1 12 2012) FALSE TRUE (Date 28 11 2012) TRUE

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Cases from none of the lives (HYPOTHETICAL).

-- An age pensioner taking a job says so in her declaration instead of quoting a number (s 202EA(2)).
#ASSERT `Is my TFN declaration effective on a day` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 1 9 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` TRUE
-- The "don't know my number, have asked the Commissioner" statement works as the pending statement does (s 202CB(2)(b)).
#ASSERT `Is my TFN declaration effective on a day` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 29 7 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` TRUE
#ASSERT `Is my TFN declaration effective on a day` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 30 7 2026) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `answered` FALSE
-- A declaration given to Centrelink as a claimant: not covered (s 202CB(6)).
#ASSERT `Is my TFN declaration effective on a day` (Date 1 7 2026) (Date 1 9 2026) TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE (Date 1 1 2026) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not covered` `a TFN declaration given as a claimant to Centrelink, the Student Assistance or Employment Secretary, the Veterans' Affairs Secretary or the Repatriation Commission is not encoded (s 202CB(6) to (8))`
